## test-sxmod, inside native-test

```
[OK] the flat dialect cannot compose two modules that both declare `add`: seed-min says duplicate function name, cc rejects gen2 C, native_aot says declared twice
[OK] two modules that each declare `add` compose through sxmod and print the same nine lines under seed-min, gen2 and native_aot
[OK] the rewrite prefixes exactly the module-level names: internal references and initialisers follow, while locals, parameters, struct fields, comments and string literals are left byte for byte
[OK] a module member is not visible unqualified: `add(2, 3)` after the pass names nothing and the compiler says so
[OK] sxmod refusals: unknown member, bare alias, duplicate alias, duplicate member, missing/unquoted path, no `from`, a late `module` line, an uppercase module name, an empty module, no module at all, `use` in a program or a module, a `module` inside a module, and a parameter or local that shadows a module name -- 16 refusals, each with a diagnostic and a non-zero exit
```

## test-trust-anchor, inside native-test

```
[OK] trust anchor pinned: selfhost/seed/sxc_seed_min.c is 2176 lines / 100919 bytes, SHA-256 e4cc34b4...1cb9, recomputed here by Sayanox itself (stdlib/crypto.sa) and compared with the tracked pin
[OK] one anchor: the seed-min rule compiles selfhost/seed/sxc_seed_min.c and nothing else; every later .c in the chain (gen1_min.c, gen2.c, gen3.c, gen4.c) is generated by the toolchain and gitignored
[OK] anchor surface: four standard headers (ctype, stdio, stdlib, string), and not one reference to system, fork, exec*, dlopen, socket, setuid, unlink, rename, chmod, remove, tmpnam or getenv -- 2176 lines a reviewer can actually read
[OK] the anchor itself never shells out: the single popen/pclose/curl site is one line of RUNTIME text it emits (sx_http, behind the http_get builtin), so every compiled program carries exactly one shell-out and the compiler carries none
[OK] anchor behaviour: compiling the 19.6k-line compiler twice gives byte-identical C, so what the anchor is trusted for is reproducible
[OK] still failing closed: `make all-sayanox` refuses the all-in-Sayanox claim, and this gate pins the exception rather than removing it -- C is still the trust anchor, now a measured one
```

